        "raw": "<p>OK, I&#39;ve played this game a lot and i camt believe this never came up before in any of our game sessions. But im confident the forum will have an answer :)</p><p>If a card says that a target deals X irreducible damage, is the end result of the damage irreducible, or only X amount?</p><p>For example, let&#39;s say there is a card that&#39;s says &quot;Mister Fixer deals a villain target 1 irreducible damage and currently there are two active actions that increase damage dealt by Mister Fixer by 1 so his total damage output is 3, but the villain has a damage reduction of 1. Does the villain:</p><p>a) take 3 damage because the entire damage instance is irreducible?</p><p>b take 2 damage because the reduction does apply to amounts higher than 1?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Follow up question:</p><p>If the original cards says &quot;Mister Fixer deals 1 target 1 irreducible melee damage, but there is an active card that increases damage dealt by Mister Fixer by 1 AND changes that damage type to fire, does it then lose its irreducibility since it is no longer melee damage (and therefore no longer matching what the original card said)?</p>",
