        "id": 70811,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-12T22:18:52.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Irreducible can be increased, but not decreased. No matter how much you increase it, it will never go back down, so Fixer would be dealing 3 damage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Alternating Tiger Claw says something along the lines that all his damage is Irreducible. So no matter what type of damage it is, it will always be irreducible if he is the one dealing the damage. And if I card ever comes into existance that changes the type of damage, I would still say it would be irreducible, as it it more of a subtype.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:49:47.602Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
