        "created_at": "2013-08-13T09:48:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>On the subject of irreducible damage, I have a quick inquiry about Plague Rat, perhaps the master of irreducible damage since he does some every turn. If he's got Twist the Ether on him, this says that Visionary can choose the type and then either increase or reduce the damage by one. It says <span class=\"bbcode-i\">either</span>, not <span class=\"bbcode-i\">may</span> (as far as I remember, unless it <span class=\"bbcode-i\">does</span> say \"may\" in which case ignore this whole question ;)), so if the damage is irreducible you can't choose to reduce it, right? So Twist can only <span class=\"bbcode-i\">increase</span> Rat's irreducible damage? And likewise if an Infected hero has Twist on them, I suppose…</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:49:47.805Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
