      {
        "id": 70816,
        "name": "ketigid",
        "username": "ketigid",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/9fc29f/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-13T14:31:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You can still choose to reduce the damage, it just wouldn't work.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>How is this different from a player choosing to destroy a card when they have no cards to destroy? One of Iron Legacy’s card I think,  I don’t have my decks now.</p>",
