        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>To me,&nbsp;choosing to destroy a card or discard a card also includes choosing the card to destroy/discard.&nbsp; So if there is no card, that is not an option.</p><p>Now, one of the disturbing things about&nbsp;&#39;ruling 15&#39;&nbsp;was that it called into question things like Twist the Ether choosing to reduce irreducible damage.&nbsp; But I think the plan is to reword the applicable cards and we can still go with the assumption that players can choose an effect (like reduce damage) even if another effect will cancel it.</p>",
        "actions_summary": [
          {
            "id": 2,
            "can_act": true
          },
          {
            "id": 6,
            "can_act": true
          },
