      {
        "id": 70818,
        "name": "ariano",
        "username": "ariano",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/67e7ee/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-27T14:54:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dypaca\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dypaca/48/2079_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dypaca:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>To me,&nbsp;choosing to destroy a card or discard a card also includes choosing the card to destroy/discard.&nbsp; So if there is no card, that is not an option.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>In other context, if an attack goes in the lines of \"the heroe with the lowest hp loses an ongoing effect\" and there are two heroes with the lowest hp, one with an ongoing effect, the other withou ongoing effects, according to rules, page 8, in case of tied hp the players chose the attacked heroe and from other post somewhere here in the forum, it was the consense that it is perfectly legal to chose the heroe without ongoing effects as the target of the attack, efectively nullying it.</p>\n<p>The same logic should apply here, I think…</p>",
        "post_number": 9,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:49:48.106Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
